WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:02.247
Our running case is a small outpatient

00:00:02.274 --> 00:00:06.309
clinic The clinic needs to track patients

00:00:06.441 --> 00:00:10.085
providers appointments services and the services
delivered

00:00:10.112 --> 00:00:14.086
during each appointment Think about which words

00:00:14.099 --> 00:00:16.678
describe independent things and which words describe

00:00:16.691 --> 00:00:21.115
relationships or rules Patient provider appointment
and

00:00:21.141 --> 00:00:24.444
service sound like candidate entities A rule

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:26.128
such as every appointment must have a

00:00:26.141 --> 00:00:30.117
provider sounds more like a constraint The

00:00:30.143 --> 00:00:32.288
design also needs to prevent problems such

00:00:32.301 --> 00:00:35.999
as duplicate patient identifiers negative prices
impossible

00:00:36.025 --> 00:00:38.420
appointment times and service lists stored as

00:00:38.433 --> 00:00:42.828
comma-separated text Before looking at the schema

00:00:43.064 --> 00:00:44.933
try a quick warm-up which words in

00:00:44.959 --> 00:00:47.393
this scenario would you initially consider tables

00:00:47.630 --> 00:00:49.617
and which would you consider business rules
